  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0133' consists of five tables: 'Book_Category', 'Reader_Category', 'Book', 'Reader', and 'Borrowing_Information'.\nThe 'Book_Category' table has two columns: 'Book_Type_ID' of type INTEGER and 'Description' of type VARCHAR(255). It also has a primary key constraint on 'Book_Type_ID'.\nThe 'Reader_Category' table has three columns: 'Description' of type VARCHAR(255), 'Reader_Type_ID' of type INTEGER, and 'Type_Name' of type VARCHAR(255). It has a primary key constraint on 'Reader_Type_ID'.\nThe 'Book' table has eight columns: 'Author' of type VARCHAR(255), 'Book_ID' of type INTEGER, 'Book_Type_ID' of type INTEGER, 'Content_Description' of type VARCHAR(255), 'Price' of type FLOAT, 'Publication_Date' of type DATETIME, 'Publisher' of type VARCHAR(255), and 'Title' of type VARCHAR(255). It has a primary key constraint on 'Book_ID' and a foreign key constraint on 'Book_Type_ID' referencing 'Book_Category' table.\nThe 'Reader' table has six columns: 'Contact_Number' of type INTEGER, 'Credit_Score' of type FLOAT, 'Description' of type VARCHAR(255), 'Reader_ID' of type INTEGER, 'Reader_Type_ID' of type INTEGER, and 'Type_Name' of type VARCHAR(255). It has a primary key constraint on 'Reader_ID' and a foreign key constraint on 'Reader_Type_ID' referencing 'Reader_Category' table.\nThe 'Borrowing_Information' table has six columns: 'Book_ID' of type INTEGER, 'Borrow_Date' of type DATETIME, 'Fine' of type FLOAT, 'Reader_ID' of type INTEGER, 'Renewal_Count' of type VARCHAR(255), and 'Return_Date' of type DATETIME. It has a primary key constraint on 'Book_ID' and 'Reader_ID' and 'Borrow_Date', and foreign key constraints on 'Book_ID' referencing 'Book' table and 'Reader_ID' referencing 'Reader' table.",
  "gold_question": "The library management system is as follows:\nThe library has multiple books, each book has a Book ID, Title, Author, Publisher, Publication Date, Price, Book Type, and Content Description.     \nBook Type information is stored in the Book Category table, which includes Book Type ID, Type Name, and Description.\nThe library has multiple readers, each reader has a Reader ID, Reader Type, Contact Number, Credit Score, and Description.\nReader Type information is stored in the Reader Category table, which includes Reader Type ID, Type Name, and Description.\nThe borrowing process is recorded in the Borrowing table, each borrowing record has a Book ID, Reader ID, Borrow Date, Return Date, Renewal Count, and Fine.\nThe system manages book borrowing and returning, as well as reader borrowing permissions and credit scores through this information.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0133.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0133\nCREATE TABLE `Book_Category` (\n  `Book_Type_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Book_Type_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Reader_Category` (\n  `Reader_Type_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Type_Name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Reader_Type_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Book` (\n  `Book_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Title` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Author` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Publisher` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Publication_Date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Price` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Content_Description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Book_Type_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Book_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `book_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Book_Type_ID`) REFERENCES `Book_Category` (`Book_Type_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Reader` (\n  `Reader_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Contact_Number` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Credit_Score` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Reader_Type_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Type_Name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Reader_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `reader_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Reader_Type_ID`) REFERENCES `Reader_Category` (`Reader_Type_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Borrowing_Information` (\n  `Book_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Reader_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Borrow_Date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `Return_Date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Fine` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Renewal_Count` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Book_ID`, `Reader_ID`, `Borrow_Date`),\n  CONSTRAINT `borrowing_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Book_ID`) REFERENCES `Book` (`Book_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `borrowing_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Reader_ID`) REFERENCES `Reader` (`Reader_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
